===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|id=comparative|:inh|enm:bettre|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|better}}, {{m|enm|bettre}}, {{m|enm|betre}}, from {{inh|en|ang|betera||better}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*batiʀō}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*batizô||better}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro||*bʰed-rós}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*bʰed-||good}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nl|beter}}, {{cog|de|besser}}, {{cog|da,nb|bedre}}, {{cog|nn|betre}}, {{cog|sv|bättre}}, {{cog|fo,is|betri}}. Also {{cog|sa|भ॒द्र||blessed; fortunate; happy; good}} (from {{m|ine-pro||*bʰn̥d-ró-s}}). Related to {{m|en|best}} and {{m|en|battle||getting better; improving; fruitful; fertile}}. Compare also {{cog|is|batna||to improve}}, {{m|is|bót||improvement}}, {{cog|de|besser}}. More at {{m|en|batten}}, {{m|en|boot}}.

{{false cognate|fa|بهتر|tr=behtar}}.

